---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import gettingStuckImage from "../../Getting Stuck - Work With Me .jpg";
import "../styles/work-with-me.css";

const formAction = "https://formspree.io/f/xwlpaqpg";
---

<BaseLayout title="Work With Me | Kali Harmen | Dare to Break Free" description="One-to-one collaboration sessions with Kali Harmen for stories, business, marketing and life transitions." pageClass="work-page">
  <section class="work-hero" aria-labelledby="work-page-title">
    <div class="work-hero__photo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="work-hero__content">
      <h1 id="work-page-title">One-to-One Collaboration Sessions</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-intro work-section" aria-label="How we might collaborate">
    <div class="work-section__inner work-intro__inner">
      <Image
        class="work-intro__image-slot"
        src={gettingStuckImage}
        alt="A notebook, pen and notes on a desk, ready for ideas"
        widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200, 1600]}
        sizes="(max-width: 600px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--page-gutter)), (max-width: 685px) 70vw, (max-width: 900px) 30rem, 45vw"
        format="webp"
        quality={82}
      />
      <div class="work-intro__copy">
        <p>If you’re caught up in something you’re trying to create or change in your life, sometimes having another brain in the room is just what you need to get things moving again.</p>
        <p>I don’t have a five-step process or promise transformation. What I do have is years of coaching, business and marketing experience, what I learnt from sticking with a memoir long enough to finish it, and a neurodivergent brain that tends to notice patterns and make connections.</p>
        <p>I’m useful when you need someone to challenge your thinking, spot what you may be missing and help you notice if you’re making yourself smaller (I think I’ve earned a PhD in that area). Of course, nothing changes unless you take some sort of action.</p>
        <p><button class="work-intro__more-trigger" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="action-dialog">More about that here.</button></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <dialog class="work-action-dialog" id="action-dialog" aria-labelledby="action-dialog-title">
    <div class="work-action-dialog__header">
      <h2 id="action-dialog-title">What happens after we talk</h2>
      <button class="work-action-dialog__close" type="button" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <div class="work-action-dialog__body">
      <p>Talking something through can be hugely useful. It can also feel like progress when, in reality, nothing has changed. Believe me, I've been there more times than I'd care to admit.</p>
      <p>That's why, when we work together, we'll look at what you're actually going to do with what we've discussed. It doesn't have to be some grand gesture or an enormous to-do list. Just something that makes sense to you and that you're willing to try. Because ultimately, if nothing changes, nothing changes.</p>
      <p>And if you don't do it? That's worth exploring too.</p>
      <p>Perhaps the action wasn't right for you, the timing was wrong, or there's something deeper going on that we haven't yet uncovered. Resistance can tell us quite a lot, and simply pushing harder isn't always the answer.</p>
      <p>I'd much rather you came back and told me what didn't feel right, challenged the suggestion or offered something you'd be prepared to do instead. That's all part of working together.</p>
      <p>What happens between our conversations gives us something real to work with next time. We can come up with all sorts of ideas in a session, but it's when you take them into your life, try things out and see what happens that we start learning what works for you.</p>
    </div>
  </dialog>

  <section class="work-areas work-section" aria-labelledby="work-areas-title">
    <div class="work-section__inner">
      <h2 id="work-areas-title">What We Might Work On</h2>
      <p class="work-areas__intro">It could be...</p>
      <div class="work-areas__grid">
        <article class="work-areas__item">
          <h3>Memoir</h3>
          <p>A memoir you want to write or are already writing.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-areas__item">
          <h3>Business</h3>
          <p>Something in your business that has you stuck.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-areas__item">
          <h3>Marketing</h3>
          <p>A marketing idea you’re trying to make clearer.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-areas__item">
          <h3>Transition</h3>
          <p>Or you’ve found yourself knee-deep in a transition, wading into the unknown and wanting someone to work through it with.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-pricing work-section" aria-labelledby="work-pricing-title">
    <div class="work-section__inner">
      <h2 id="work-pricing-title">The practicalities</h2>
      <div class="work-pricing__grid">
        <article class="work-pricing__card">
          <div class="work-pricing__card-top">
            <h3>One-off</h3>
            <p class="work-pricing__price">£95</p>
          </div>
          <p>A 90-minute session for something contained enough that we can make useful progress in one conversation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="work-pricing__card">
          <div class="work-pricing__card-top">
            <h3>Series</h3>
            <p class="work-pricing__price">£270</p>
          </div>
          <p>Three 90-minute sessions, usually spread over six weeks, for something that needs developing, testing or revisiting over time.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-start work-section" id="enquiry" aria-labelledby="work-start-title">
    <div class="work-section__inner work-start__inner">
      <div class="work-start__copy">
        <h2 id="work-start-title">Getting started</h2>
        <p>Start by filling out a short form so I can understand what you’re working on and where you’re getting stuck.</p>
        <p>From there, we can have a free 20-minute scoping call to see if we’re a good fit to collaborate and whether I’m the right person for what you need. There’s no obligation to go any further.</p>
        <p>If the stars align, we’ll agree what to work on and book our first session.</p>
      </div>
        <div class="work-start__form-wrap">
        <h3>Tell me what you’re working on</h3>
          <form class="contact-form work-start__form" action={formAction} method="POST">
            <div class="contact-form__honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
              <label for="work-website">Leave this field empty</label>
              <input id="work-website" name="_gotcha" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
            </div>
            <label for="work-name">Name</label>
            <input id="work-name" type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required />
            <label for="work-email">Email</label>
            <input id="work-email" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required />
            <label for="work-message">What are you working on, and where are you getting stuck?</label>
            <textarea id="work-message" name="message" rows="5" required></textarea>
            <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="work-with-me" />
            <button class="button" type="submit">Send enquiry</button>
            <p class="form-privacy-notice">Your details are used to respond to your enquiry. See the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
          </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    const actionDialog = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>("#action-dialog");
    const actionDialogTrigger = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".work-intro__more-trigger");
    const actionDialogClose = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".work-action-dialog__close");

    actionDialogTrigger?.addEventListener("click", () => actionDialog?.showModal());
    actionDialogClose?.addEventListener("click", () => actionDialog?.close());
    actionDialog?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
      if (event.target === actionDialog) actionDialog.close();
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
